page('costs.html','The cost of keeping','OPERATING COSTS / 07','No property-specific premium, utility bill or repair allowance can be verified from a ZIP-code average.',table('Actual expense register · blank means unverified or withheld, never zero',['Category','Verified annual amount','Status / research finding','Official context'],costs,'unverified')+'''<h2>Insurance research result</h2><p>The California Department of Insurance provides premium and coverage comparison tools and recommends shopping policies. Those tools do not establish a binding primary-home or mixed-use landlord premium without building, coverage, claims and occupancy details. No official quote was obtained, so none is filled in. FAIR Plan coverage is limited; separate difference-in-conditions coverage may be needed. Do not budget only a generic online average.</p><details><summary>Historic assessment / tax verification register · no actual bill data published</summary>'''+table('Property A · supplied historical years, amounts not officially verified',['Year','Property tax','Assessment','Status','Official context'],history_a,'unverified')+table('Property B · supplied historical years, amounts not officially verified',['Year','Property tax','Assessment','Status','Official context'],history_b,'unverified')+'''</details>'''+notice('From gross rent to cash flow','Collected rent − tax − insurance − owner utilities − repairs − management − capital cash outlays − debt service − income taxes. Taxable rental profit differs because depreciation is noncash, principal repayment is not generally deductible rental expense, and improvements may be capitalized. Allocate mixed-use costs correctly; check passive-loss restrictions.')+'''<p>See <a href="projection.html">annual synthetic expense examples</a> and <a href="decision.html">after-tax cash and sensitivity illustrations</a>. They do not replace this blank actual-cost register.</p>''')

questions=[
('Trust and title','Does the trust transfer A to the intended beneficiary, and what rights or conditions apply?','Unknown; a trust does not itself establish ownership, tax inclusion or basis.','Counsel privately examines the complete trust, amendments and current title.','trustbasis'),
('Family-home exclusion','Are the relationship, transferor residence and beneficiary occupancy requirements met?','Unknown; moving in alone does not establish eligibility.','Ask the county assessor and counsel to review facts and current BOE claims before the deadline.','boe'),
('Values and taxes','What are the current fair market values, factored bases, direct charges and transfer-date supplemental taxes?','Unknown; no verified parcel-specific figures published.','Obtain assessor records and a qualified appraisal privately; reconcile the tax bill and exemptions.','rtc'),
('Estate tax and liquidity','What assets, debts, prior taxable gifts, deductions and portability are relevant?','Unknown; neither the taxable estate nor remaining exemption is established.','Estate counsel and a tax professional inventory assets and review prior returns and Form 706.','estate'),
('Income tax basis','Does A qualify for a basis adjustment, and what is B’s adjusted basis?','Unknown; property-tax assessment is not income-tax basis.','Review trust inclusion, acquisition and improvement records and obtain a date-of-death appraisal.','basis'),
('Rental economics','What rents are legal and achievable; what are vacancy, management, tax and capital costs?','Unknown; existing rent is not a new benefit of inheritance.','Privately review leases, local rules, inspections and independent property-manager estimates.','rent'),
('Insurance and utilities','What will actual coverage, water, solar true-up and other utilities cost in each use?','Unknown; estimates or solar credits are not binding quotes or guaranteed profits.','Obtain occupancy-specific policies and a full year of bills and tariff/solar agreements privately.','insurance'),
('B housing and rentals','Which space can be occupied or lawfully rented, and what changes if the Inheritor moves?','Unknown; do not assume new rent or alter common income without evidence.','Review permits, leases, occupancy and applicable local rules with counsel.','tenantlaw'),
('Investment and risk','What time horizon, liquidity reserve, tax situation and tolerance for losses apply?','Unknown; a return assumption is not a verified outcome.','Compare after-tax diversified alternatives and cash reserves with a fiduciary adviser.','sec')]
gates=[
('Gate 1','Is the inherited home legally and practically transferable to the Inheritor?','Trust terms, current title, debts, any conditions or co-beneficiaries, and who has authority to act.','Trust document, amendments, deed and trustee correspondence, read privately by counsel.','Unblocks everything else: no path can be evaluated until ownership is established.','trustbasis'),
('Gate 2','Are the family-home conditions actually met?','Eligible relationship, transferor principal residence, transferee move-in within one year, and the exemption claim filed first.','Counsel and the county assessor review facts against BOE Publication 800-1 and the claim forms.','Decides whether the old assessment can continue or the home is reassessed at market value; this is the largest single cost lever.','boepub'),
('Gate 3','What is the value and basis on the transfer date?','Date-of-death fair market value, alternate-valuation eligibility, adjusted basis of the already-owned home, and any basis-consistency reporting.','A qualified appraisal plus acquisition and improvement records, reviewed by a tax preparer.','Determines the gain if the home is sold and the depreciation if it is rented.','basis'),
('Gate 4','Does the estate exceed the federal exclusion, and is there liquidity?','Gross estate, prior taxable gifts, deductions, portability, and the exclusion in force at the transfer year.','A confidential estate inventory and Form 706 analysis by estate counsel and a tax professional.','An estate-tax or liquidity problem can force a sale regardless of which path is preferred.','estate'),
('Gate 5','What would each path actually cash-flow?','Verified achievable rent, vacancy, management, lawful unit status, insurance quote, water, electricity or solar true-up, repairs and capital reserve.','Leases, a full year of bills, a tariff or solar agreement, inspection, and occupancy-specific insurance quotes, collected privately.','Turns the rent and live-in paths from concepts into comparable numbers.','cdires'),
('Gate 6','Which path wins on the same end date, after tax and after risk?','After-tax liquidation wealth at one horizon, liquidity reserve, concentration, and tolerance for loss.','The household’s own comparison using the evidence from Gates 1 to 5, reviewed with a fiduciary adviser.','The only step that produces a decision; everything above is evidence gathering.','sec')]
page('questions.html','Questions before deciding','DECISION READINESS / 08','A checklist for discovering missing information without publishing private records.',notice('Answer in order','The gates below are sequential: a later gate cannot be answered honestly while an earlier one is open. Each row names the evidence that closes it and the page that explains the rule. Nothing here asks you to submit a document to this site.')+table('Decision gates in order · what must be true before a decision is reasonable',['Gate','Question to settle','What is needed','How to obtain it privately','Why it comes here','Official context'],gates,'unverified')+table('Questions, current answers and suggested evidence · links supply context, not proof of household facts',['Question','What needs answering','Current answer','How to discover','Official context'],questions,'unverified')+notice('Keep answers private','Use a secure channel with the trustee and licensed advisers. Do not upload deeds, bills, names, addresses, account balances or completed answers to this public site or repository.'))

def review_controls(key):
    """Local radio choices only; no form, script, persistence or network submission."""
    options = [('adopt','Adopt'),('hold','Hold'),('reject','Reject')]
    controls = ''.join(
        '<label for="%s-%s"><input id="%s-%s" type="radio" name="review-%s" value="%s"%s> %s</label>' %
        (key, value, key, value, key, value, ' checked' if value == 'hold' else '', label)
        for value,label in options)
    return '<fieldset class="review-choice"><legend>Review only</legend>'+controls+'</fieldset>'


suggestions=[
('1 · Private decision workspace','Create an access-controlled offline or securely hosted model with reviewed inputs and documented assumptions.','Reduces public exposure and allows actual after-tax comparison. Requires a real access-control and security review; never treat noindex as privacy.',review_controls('s1'),'history'),
('2 · Evidence ledger','Track each private input, document, verification date and unresolved issue; separate assumptions from facts.','Makes decisions auditable without publishing records. Needs adviser and document access.',review_controls('s2'),'estate'),
('3 · Comparable outcomes','Compare all choices at the same transfer dates and horizons, with taxes, debt, occupancy changes, capital costs and liquidity.','Makes trade-offs visible. Requires verified basis, quotes, lawful rents and personal priorities.',review_controls('s3'),'rent'),
('4 · Scenario dashboard','Add editable private assumptions, inflation-adjusted results and correlated recession, insurance, utility and tax shocks.','Exposes sensitivity rather than implying a precise forecast. Requires independent model tests; hypothetical rates are not official.',review_controls('s4'),'sec'),
('5 · Decision checkpoints','Create reminders for trustee notice, BOE-266 before BOE-19-P, occupancy and federal filing/payment.','Reduces missed deadlines; BOE Pub. 800-1 describes the Prop 19 residence and claim deadlines; verify the date-specific rule before relying on it.',review_controls('s5'),'boepub'),
('6 · Law and source monitoring','Periodically recheck official federal, state and local authorities and distinguish enacted changes from proposals.','Avoids stale law; P.L. 119-21 sets 1% annual SALT-cap increases through 2029 and a $10,000 cap thereafter unless changed by later law.',review_controls('s6'),'saltlaw'),
('7 · Close the gates in order','Work through the six decision gates on the Open questions page before collecting anything else, so no evidence is gathered for a path that a legal gate already excludes.','Stops wasted effort and stops a cost comparison being built on an ownership or eligibility assumption that later fails.',review_controls('s7'),'boepub'),
('8 · Quote pack, one request per category','Request written quotes in a single pass: three occupancy-specific insurance quotes, a written water and electricity tariff summary, one inspection with a repair and capital reserve schedule, and two independent rental estimates.','Replaces estimates with dated evidence and makes the three paths comparable on the same terms. Never send these documents to this site.',review_controls('s8'),'cdires'),
('9 · Publish the decision rule before the numbers','Agree in writing what would make the household choose each path before the figures arrive, so the outcome is not reverse-engineered from one projection.','Reduces anchoring on a single forecast and makes the later choice auditable.',review_controls('s9'),'sec')]
