issues=[
('I01','Personal records and Git history','The repository is public and its history holds earlier editions written before the figures were rounded. Pages exclusion does not remove them; forks, caches, clones and pull-request references may persist.','Owner decision: make the repository private and/or rewrite history with coordination, or accept the exposure.','history'),
('I02','2026 SALT amount not on the linked page','The 2026 personal state and local tax figure could not be confirmed from the linked 2025 instructions; only the 2025 amount, the phase-down and the floor were verified.','Re-read the IRS release for the 2026 amount and how it applies to itemizers, before relying on any 2026 figure.','sched_a'),
('I03','Name of the 1% California surtax','RTC §17043 imposes the tax, but the renaming used on current FTB forms was not re-verified in this pass, so the guide states the tax and cites the statute only.','Re-check the current Form 540 instructions before quoting a label in any filing discussion.','t117043'),
('I04','Ballot results are unofficial','Returns read on 13 November 2026 are unofficial until certification, due by 11 December 2026, and no property-tax measure on that ballot changed the transfer rules.','Re-read the certified results if any ballot outcome is used in an argument.','sos26'),
('I05','Future exclusion amount','Only 2026 and 2027 federal exclusion amounts are published. A transfer in 2040 to 2050 depends on law that does not exist yet.','Model the estate at several exclusion levels; do not project a single statutory number.','irs27'),
('I06','Prop 19 allowance after February 2027','The adjusted allowance is published only through 15 February 2027 and is indexed every other year by a California house-price index.','Re-read the BOE notice in force at the transfer date; never carry the current allowance forward.','allow'),
('I07','Family-home eligibility facts','Relationship, transferor residence, transferee move-in and continuing occupancy are private facts, and any of them can fail.','Counsel and the assessor confirm them in writing before the claim; failure means reassessment at market value.','boepub'),
('I08','Date of change in ownership per property','For the inherited home the death is the change-in-ownership date, not the distribution date; the already-owned home keeps its own assessment track.','Confirm both dates with counsel and the assessor so no filing window is missed.','boepub'),
('I09','Basis of each property','The inherited home generally takes date-of-death value, but trust inclusion and reporting rules can alter the result; the already-owned home keeps its own adjusted basis.','A date-of-death appraisal plus acquisition and improvement records; review Revenue Ruling 2023-2 with counsel.','trustbasis'),
('I10','Whether the estate is inside or outside the federal exclusion','No estate inventory, prior-gift history, deduction schedule, citizenship determination or portability election has been established.','A confidential inventory and Form 706 analysis; remember the filing threshold and the actual liability are different questions.','estate'),
('I11','Sale proceeds after tax','Offers, debt, commissions, recording costs, transfer taxes, estate allocations and the gain calculation are all unverified, and a gain may span both federal and California ordinary rates.','Obtain real offers and a tax projection before comparing sale with rent.','sell'),
('I12','Rent that is lawful and achievable','Existing income from the already-owned home is not new income from the inheritance, and any new tenancy must be lawful, insured and priced realistically.','Leases, permits, local rules and an independent management estimate.','tenantlaw'),
('I13','Insurance quotes for each use','No property-specific premium exists for a primary residence, a landlord policy or a mixed-occupancy building; averages are not quotes and standard policies exclude earthquake, flood and long vacancy.','Occupancy-specific quotes with replacement cost, deductible and liability stated, plus separate earthquake and flood decisions.','cdires'),
('I14','Water, electricity and solar after transfer','Bills, provider, tariff, fixed charges, annual true-up and whether any solar credit or legacy tariff transfers are all unverified; a credit is not a cash profit.','A full year of bills, the tariff or interconnection agreement, and provider confirmation of transfer treatment.','cpuc'),
('I15','Repairs, capital work and a reserve','Routine deductible repairs, capital improvements and a replacement reserve have not been separated or quantified.','An inspection and a documented reserve schedule; treat improvements as capital, not repairs.','rent'),
('I16','Local direct charges and special assessments','City and special-district charges, parcel assessments and any supplemental bill are parcel-specific and were not verified.','Current tax bill, assessor records and the local tax-rate area.','boe'),
('I17','Investment returns and taxes on reinvestment','Any assumed return is an assumption, not evidence; taxes on gains, dividends and liquidation reduce the comparison.','Use several return and tax scenarios; show results after all taxes and fees.','sec'),
('I18','Sequence and concentration risk','Two homes in one region is concentrated exposure; a simultaneous housing and market loss cannot be solved by selling either asset at the bottom.','Run a correlated stress case before committing to either concentration.','recession'),
('I19','Housing need and preference','Whether moving into the inherited home actually replaces other housing cost is a private fact; assigning it a value would be invention.','Decide the intended housing use explicitly and record it as an assumption.','sec'),
('I20','Selling the already-owned home','Selling or changing the use of the already-owned home is a separate decision with its own tax and rent consequences and is out of scope here.','Handle it as its own analysis if it becomes a real option.','sell'),
('I21','Local rent regulation','Statewide rent limits have statutory exemptions, and local rules may be stricter; applicability to a specific building is unverified.','Counsel or a local rent programme confirms coverage before setting any rent.','tenantlaw'),
('I22','Legal entity and titling of any rental','Holding the home personally, in trust or in an entity has different liability, tax and property-tax consequences that were not assessed.','Estate and tax counsel review before any titling change, which can itself trigger reassessment.','boe'),
('I23','Water system and wastewater provider','An address lookup identifies a drinking-water system but does not verify rates, and wastewater may be a different provider.','Identify both providers from current bills and read each adopted rate schedule.','water'),
('I24','Pending and future law','No exhaustive search of pending legislation, local measures or future federal proposals was performed, and future law is unknowable.','Re-check BOE, the Legislature, the county and federal guidance at the time of action.','boe')]
page('issues.html','Issues to resolve','EVIDENCE GAPS / 10','Every open question this analysis found, ordered by what it blocks, with the evidence that would close it and who can supply it.',notice('How to use this page','Nothing here is a decision. Rows are open questions: each one names what is unknown, what would settle it, and the official context. A row disappears only when the evidence exists privately, not when it is published here.')+table('Open items · status is unverified by design, never zero and never assumed',['ID','Open item','Why it matters / what is unresolved','What would close it','Official context'],issues,'unverified')+notice('What would make this page shorter','Verified private records: the trust and deed, the assessor records and bills, a date-of-death appraisal, occupancy-specific insurance quotes, a year of utility bills, the solar or tariff agreement, and an estate inventory. Each closes one or more rows. None of them should be uploaded to this public site or repository.'))


